{"name":"Sleep Baby Sleep","hex":"#bed1e1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sleep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rest in a state of reduced consciousness.","To have sexual intercourse (see sleep with)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of reduced consciousness during which a human or animal rests in a daily rhythm.","An act or instance of sleeping."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sleep"},{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.","Any very young animal, especially a vertebrate; many species have specific names for their babies, such as kittens for the babies of cats, puppies for the babies of dogs, and chicks for the babies of birds. See Category:Baby animals for more."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sleep","blocks":[{"text":"Sleep is a state of reduced mental and physical activity in which consciousness is altered and certain sensory activity is inhibited. During sleep, there is a marked decrease in muscle activity and interactions with the surrounding environment. While sleep differs from wakefulness in terms of the ability to react to stimuli, it still involves active brain patterns, making it more reactive than a coma or disorders of consciousness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg/330px-Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sleep"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg/500px-Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg/500px-Domenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sleeping Girl, Domenico Fetti, c. 1615","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADomenico_Fetti_-_Sleeping_Girl_-_WGA7863.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/1900_The_Awakening.jpg/500px-1900_The_Awakening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/1900_The_Awakening.jpg/500px-1900_The_Awakening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"The Awakening\", an illustration to writing by Leo Tolstoy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1900_The_Awakening.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png/250px-Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/33/Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png/250px-Pillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Pillow height during side sleeping affects the spine and neck muscles. See Sleep and musculoskeletal health.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APillow_Height_in_Side-Lying_Position.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Noon%2C_rest_from_work_-_Van_Gogh.jpeg/500px-Noon%2C_rest_from_work_-_Van_Gogh.jpeg?utm_sourc